menu "BMDS storage"

    config BMDS_STORAGE_STACK_BYTES
        int "Storage task stack size (bytes, PSRAM)"
        default 6144
        range 3072 65536
        help
            Stack of the storage service task, which handles card insertion
            and removal (card initialization, and later mounting). In PSRAM.
            Check the 'tasks' command's stack_free column before shrinking.

    config BMDS_STORAGE_PRIORITY
        int "Storage task priority"
        default 3
        range 1 24
        help
            FreeRTOS priority of the storage task. Above the shell, so a
            removed card is noticed while a command is busy.

    config BMDS_SD_MAX_KHZ
        int "SD card bus clock limit (kHz)"
        default 40000
        range 400 40000
        help
            Highest SD bus clock. 40000 is high speed (about 20 MB/s on a
            4-bit bus) for cards that support it; others stay at the default
            speed, 20000. Lower it to rule out signal problems.

    config BMDS_SD_BOUNCE_BYTES
        int "SD bounce buffer size (bytes, PSRAM)"
        default 65536
        range 512 65536
        help
            DMA-capable buffer that requests in buffers the SD host can't
            reach by DMA (unaligned, or not DMA-capable) are copied through,
            so the driver never allocates per request. A multiple of 512.
            Larger is faster for such requests (one card command a buffer):
            reading a file through the VFS 4.9 MB/s at 4 KB, 9.4 at 32 KB,
            10.1 at 64 KB (devplan/bench.md §19). Aligned PSRAM buffers
            don't use it.

    config BMDS_ZONEINFO_PATH
        string "Time zone database"
        default "/sd0/p0/share/zoneinfo.bin"
        help
            The time zone database (one file, built by tools/bmds-dist as
            the tzdata package), shown to programs as /share/zoneinfo and
            used for zone names in clock/zone, CONFIG_BMDS_TIMEZONE and
            TZ. The default of the system configuration's clock/tzdata,
            which 'sysconf' changes at run time.

    config BMDS_LEAPSECONDS_PATH
        string "Leap-second list"
        default "/sd0/p0/share/leap-seconds.list"
        help
            IANA's leap-seconds.list (the tzdata package's), for CLOCK_TAI and PTP's UTC
            offset (devplan/network.md §31e). The ROM's /rom/share/leap-seconds.list is used
            while none is there, or when it expires later. The default of the system
            configuration's clock/leapseconds.

endmenu
